  (text "TPS7A0230PDBVR = 3.0V 200mA LDO for the microSD, switched by SD_EN\nC34 1u on IN = \"1uF or greater\" @ DS p27\nC35 1u on OUT: needs >= 0.5uF effective, <= 22uF derated @ DS p5. with C40/C41 = 4.7u typ (calc)\nEN: >= 1.1V = on, <= 0.3V = off, 60R discharge when off @ DS p7\ninternal EN pulldown is DISCONNECTED once EN was driven high @ DS p3\n-> R20 1M so EN falls LOW when P0.14 floats = after every MCU reset @ PS p90\n+-1.5% @ DS p6 = a row for IN >= 3.5V. dropout 310mV max at 200mA @ DS p6 + p7\nNEVER let the charger pull SYS down: current BACK through this LDO @ DS p19 (README F1)"
    (at 20.32 100.33 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "538e2474-b16f-44ad-8e07-fd3394e6d42a")
  )
  (text "microSD in SPI mode: CS = DAT3, DI = CMD, DO = DAT0, SCK = CLK @ SD spec p38 table 3-1\n16MHz MAX, default speed ONLY: high speed may take 200mA @ SD spec p50 = all the LDO gives (README F6)\nR12-R16 10k pullups on DAT2, CS, CMD, DAT0, DAT1. value NOT stated by the Simplified spec @ SD spec p306\npullups to 3V0_SD, not VDD: nothing may feed an unpowered card through its pins @ SD spec p301\nR21 10k pulldown on SCK: P0.19 floats after every MCU reset @ PS p370, LOW = what an unpowered card wants\nC40 10u + C41 100n at the socket: rail should rise in 0.1 to 35ms @ SD spec p301. value NOT stated @ SD spec p306\ndetect switch: no card = closed, card in = open @ TF-110 drawing p1 -> wired so no card = LOW\nNO pullup fitted: firmware turns on the P0.16 pullup ONLY while sampling (README F5)\ncard power up / down sequence = README F5"
    (at 144.78 110.49 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "62f52eca-55e2-45dd-b5dc-c9f267b7d698")
  )
